WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.305
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Wednesday, November fourth.

2
00:00:04.305 --> 00:00:07.122
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.122 --> 00:00:13.049
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:15.673
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:15.673 --> 00:00:20.925
Another tanker was struck off northern Oman, and Iran's Revolutionary Guard claims four tankers hit mines near the Strait of Hormuz.

6
00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:27.997
The remnants of Cyclone Murasu are still bringing extremely heavy rain to southern India.

7
00:00:27.997 --> 00:00:32.373
And in Saudi Arabia, the US security alert stands, with Riyadh flights still being cancelled.

8
00:00:32.373 --> 00:00:34.842
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:37.850
Gulf shipping.

10
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:46.285
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: late on Tuesday, a tanker about fourteen nautical miles off Oman's northern tip was struck by two unknown projectiles in the engine room.

11
00:00:46.285 --> 00:00:49.601
No casualties or environmental impact were reported.

12
00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:58.823
Also confirmed by UKMTO, citing the Indian government: an Indian crewed dhow was attacked while sailing out through the Strait of Hormuz on Monday.

13
00:00:58.823 --> 00:01:01.646
Oman's navy rescued the surviving crew.

14
00:01:01.646 --> 00:01:04.629
Trade press reports one crew member was killed.

15
00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:09.864
UKMTO published that warning about a day after the attack; reporting can lag.

16
00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:16.007
Separately, Iran's Revolutionary Guard says four tankers that ignored its rules hit mines in the strait and are burning.

17
00:01:16.007 --> 00:01:18.573
That is a claim only.

18
00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:25.064
The vessels have not been identified, and as of this brief UKMTO has issued no warning matching it.

19
00:01:25.064 --> 00:01:31.377
The latest joint maritime threat update, issued before these incidents, rates the Strait of Hormuz severe and the Gulf of Oman moderate.

20
00:01:31.377 --> 00:01:36.658
Tuesday's tanker strike was on the Gulf of Oman side.

21
00:01:36.658 --> 00:01:45.462
Tueri suggests operators with voyages near the strait review routing against the current assessment, and plan for possible escalation without assuming it.

22
00:01:45.462 --> 00:01:46.368
India.

23
00:01:46.368 --> 00:01:56.237
Confirmed by the India Meteorological Department: what is left of Cyclone Murasu has weakened into a low pressure area over Telangana and coastal Andhra Pradesh.

24
00:01:56.237 --> 00:02:03.348
Extremely heavy rain was recorded there in the twenty-four hours to Wednesday morning, and more very heavy rain is possible today.

25
00:02:03.348 --> 00:02:16.917
Reported, per state disaster officials quoted by Indian media: two people have died, more than twelve thousand people are in relief centres, more than two hundred mobile towers were affected, and more than thirty-five trains were cancelled.

26
00:02:16.917 --> 00:02:25.297
Power companies say supply is largely restored in one coastal district; that is the operators' account, and some areas remain without power.

27
00:02:25.297 --> 00:02:34.477
Tueri suggests organizations with people in the region confirm staff welfare, and check flooding and road conditions before any movement.

28
00:02:34.477 --> 00:02:35.458
Saudi Arabia.

29
00:02:35.458 --> 00:02:46.136
Confirmed: the US State Department on Tuesday restated Monday's US Mission security alert, warning of potential attacks on airports, possible airspace closures, and flight cancellations.

30
00:02:46.136 --> 00:02:47.667
It is not a new warning.

31
00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:54.229
The ordered departure of some US staff and the US travel advisory are unchanged since October twenty-third.

32
00:02:54.229 --> 00:03:01.410
At about two thirty p.m. local time today, Flightradar twenty-four showed about fifteen percent of Riyadh flights cancelled.

33
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.575
Yesterday's count used a different base, so no trend can be drawn.

34
00:03:05.575 --> 00:03:13.790
Tueri suggests travelers keep flexible plans and confirm each flight with the airline before leaving for the airport.

35
00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.069
Operations check.

36
00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:21.024
Borders and health: the US Ebola attestation rule has been in force since eleven fifty-nine p.m.

37
00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:23.939
Eastern on Tuesday.

38
00:03:23.939 --> 00:03:26.954
CDC shows no new change to the rule.

39
00:03:26.954 --> 00:03:28.402
Travelers who do not attest will be denied boarding.

40
00:03:28.402 --> 00:03:39.207
Nigeria's health portal confirms a pre-boarding declaration for all arrivals; a reported twenty-one day follow-up is still not confirmed with the authority.

41
00:03:39.207 --> 00:03:45.839
Britain's Foreign Office updated its Madagascar advice: arrivals must declare recent travel history and may be screened for Ebola.

42
00:03:45.839 --> 00:03:47.022
It does not say when that began.

43
00:03:47.022 --> 00:03:53.656
Aviation: Warsaw's second airport resumed operations on Tuesday after a bomb threat closure, its operator says.

44
00:03:53.656 --> 00:04:04.134
Infrastructure: Cloudflare measured internet traffic in Ukraine's Zhytomyr region down about fifty percent from Tuesday evening, after damage to energy facilities cut power.

45
00:04:04.134 --> 00:04:12.183
Security, reported per Reuters: Latvia says two drones violated its airspace, one believed Russian and one Ukrainian.

46
00:04:12.183 --> 00:04:20.267
Maritime: UKMTO has reclassified last week's boarding of a large fishing vessel off the Horn of Africa as a hijack; authorities fear it may support pirate attacks.

47
00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:25.836
Hazards, reported per Philippine media: Mayon volcano remains at alert level three.

48
00:04:25.836 --> 00:04:28.875
That's today's brief.

49
00:04:28.875 --> 00:04:30.333
Current as of six a.m.

50
00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:32.424
Central, Wednesday.

51
00:04:32.424 --> 00:04:33.295
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

52
00:04:33.295 --> 00:04:40.212
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

53
00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.585
Check the original source before you act.

54
00:04:42.585 --> 00:04:51.439
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

55
00:04:51.439 --> 00:04:54.097
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

56
00:04:54.097 --> 00:04:55.212
Thanks for listening.
